  "description": "YETTID crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R -3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C81 H80 Dy6 N24 O31,12(C1 H4 O1),9(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.976-4.031 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 109.31-113.39°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy6(μ4-CO3)3(μ3-OH2)(spch)6(MeOH)6(H2O)3]·4MeOH·3H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
